[h2]Core Features[/h2]

[b]1. In-Game F10 Control Center (7 Tabs)[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Tab 1 - Quick Actions & Presets:[/b] One-click automated sweeps, manual area cleanups, launcher RAM boosters, and custom profile management (Potato Mode, Balanced, Max Quality, and User Custom Presets).
[*] [b]Tab 2 - General & Engine:[/b] Dynamic Multi-Story Building Occlusion Culling, Skeletal Animation LOD blending limits, Zombie 2D Imposter rendering, and low-spec lighting rates.
[*] [b]Tab 3 - Vehicles:[/b] Anti-stutter high-speed chunk streamer, parked vehicle Bullet physics sleeping, driving priority lighting, and headlight shadow management.
[*] [b]Tab 4 - Blood & Corpses:[/b] Smart blood decal stacking cap (max 4 per tile to eliminate GPU overdraw while keeping full gore), automated corpse decay sweeps, and safe base radius exclusion.
[*] [b]Tab 5 - World Debris:[/b] Safe ground item sweeps (removes broken glass, cans, rotten food, and litter while strictly preserving player bases, safehouses, generators, tools, and backpacks).
[*] [b]Tab 6 - Audio & Climate:[/b] Screen-space dynamic puddle shader toggles, rain splash particle clamps, animal pen audio limits, burning zombie scream throttles, and fly sound emitter caps.
[*] [b]Tab 7 - Mod Profiler & Shield:[/b] Real-time mod execution monitor, 3rd-party GC freeze interceptor, log I/O spam throttler, and vehicle mechanics null-recipe crash shields.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/prop11/PZO-Launcher/Unstable/docs/gifs/02_multithreading_core_offload.gif[/img]

[b]2. Integrated High-Performance GLSL Shaders[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Lightweight Screen-Space Puddles:[/b] Replaces heavy multi-octave Perlin noise iterations with a streamlined specular pass, cutting GPU fillrate load by up to 40% during rain.
[*] [b]Low-Overhead Foliage & Wind Shader:[/b] Simplifies trigonometric vertex calculations for tree wind sway to prevent framerate drops in dense forests.
[*] [b]Optimized Rain Streaks:[/b] Single-pass alpha blend that renders clean rain cascades without multi-layer particle lag.
[/list]

[b]3. Dynamic Multi-Story Building Occlusion Culling[/b]
[list]
[*] Automatically clamps vertical rendering on upper floors (Z >= 2) to eliminate off-screen floor draw calls with zero-stutter transitions near windows, stairs, and balconies.
[/list]

[b]4. Combat Burst & Shotgun Impact Smoother[/b]
[list]
[*] Buffers blood splats and multi-kill gore across adjacent frames, eliminating the classic frame-freeze when firing shotguns into large hordes.
[/list]

[b]5. Parked Vehicle Bullet Physics Sleeping[/b]
[list]
[*] Puts stationary, unoccupied vehicles into low-overhead physics sleep mode, waking them up instantly when approached or entered.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/prop11/PZO-Launcher/Unstable/docs/gifs/04_vehicle_road_streaming.gif[/img]

[b]6. ModShield 3rd-Party Mod Protection[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]GC Interceptor:[/b] Prevents 3rd-party mods from triggering 300ms Stop-The-World garbage collection freezes during active combat and driving.
[*] [b]Log Disk Throttler:[/b] Throttles runaway informational log spam to prevent disk write stalls while preserving 100% of errors and tracebacks.
[*] [b]Vehicle Mechanics Crash Shield:[/b] Automatically sanitizes malformed vehicle repair recipes from 3rd-party mods in Build 42, preventing NullPointerException crashes in vehicle mechanics menus.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/prop11/PZO-Launcher/Unstable/docs/gifs/05_gc_freeze_shield.gif[/img]

[b]7. Main Menu Integration & Preset System[/b]
[list]
[*] Access the full Control Center directly from the Main Menu via the top-right button, with custom preset saving and update notices.
[/list]

